// Conquered ground, and the ways out of holding it (Scripts/Simulation/ConquestAftermath.cs,
// RegionalAutonomy.cs, UnionCohesion.cs).
//
// The owner's game of 17 November 2026: Serbia took Yugoslavia, proclaimed it, took Bulgaria, and
// was strangled by risings - "several times in a row on the same lands". Measured (SimBench
// --conquest serbia, docs/design/gameplay-2026-11-17/conquest-aftermath.md): a proclaimed Yugoslavia
// began at cohesion 0.40, under the union's trouble line, and counted Croats and Bosniaks as
// foreigners; conquered regions stayed at stability 0.15-0.30 for ever because nothing let their
// people get used to the new state; a crushed rising came back exactly as angry as it left and rose
// again the day its two years of protection ran out. These numbers are the way out, each with a
// price and a time. docs/CONQUEST_AFTERMATH_2026_11_17_RU.md has the before and after.
{
  // ---- acceptance: conquered ground digested by years of quiet.
  // What a quiet week adds. 0.001 is about nineteen years from nothing to home - a generation, and
  // half of the fifty years foreign ground needed before. 0 switches acceptance off.
  "AcceptanceWeekly": 0.001,
  // A people of the holder's own family of peoples ("group" in cultures/00_cultures.json) accepts
  // half as fast again: for Serbia the Yugoslav peoples and the Bulgarians alike.
  "AcceptanceKindredFactor": 1.5,
  // Full pace at or below this radicalism, none at or above the stall line (the same 0.5 that stops
  // BorderHabit): a region half radical is not getting used to anybody.
  "AcceptanceCalmRadicalism": 0.15,
  "AcceptanceStallRadicalism": 0.50,
  // A fully accepted region pays half of what its minority costs in stability and radicalism, not
  // none of it: Wales is still Wales.
  "AcceptanceMinorityRelief": 0.5,
  // And weighs 0.4 of what it did in imperial overstretch; at acceptance 1 it becomes homeland and
  // leaves the overstretch altogether.
  "AcceptanceOverstretchRelief": 0.6,
  // Ground handed over by agreement (a deal, a union, a release) arrives half accepted.
  "AcceptancePeacefulStart": 0.5,
  // A crushed rising halves what acceptance the region had: being beaten is not agreeing.
  "AcceptanceRisingKeep": 0.5,

  // ---- a crushed rising exhausts its region.
  // Its radicalism is halved the day the breakaway that held it is beaten: crushed regions came back
  // at 0.43-0.99 and rose again the day RevoltRecovery's 730 days ended.
  "RisingCrushedRadicalismCut": 0.5,
  // For three years grievance, overstretch and occupation feed its anger at 0.35 of the rate: a
  // region at 0.70 is at 0.35 the day it is retaken and at 0.15-0.20 three years on, instead of
  // full when the protection ends. Not a new immunity: RevoltRecovery stays the only guard.
  "RisingExhaustionDays": 1095,
  "RisingExhaustionInflow": 0.35,

  // ---- regional autonomy: the one active lever, the same for the computer.
  // A third of a mobilisation decision in political points, at once.
  "AutonomyPoliticalCost": 15,
  // Every week the region keeps this share of its own taxes (its share of the people times the
  // country's weekly tax income). Sixteen autonomous Yugoslav regions would cost Serbia about 30 %.
  "AutonomyRevenueShare": 0.4,
  // An autonomous region weighs as little in the overstretch as the calmest conquered one.
  "AutonomyOverstretchWeight": 0.4,
  // Self-government: less to resent, and twice as fast to accept the state.
  "AutonomyRadicalismInflow": 0.6,
  "AutonomyAcceptanceFactor": 2.0,
  // Taking it back is free and remembered: +10 points of radicalism at once, half the acceptance
  // gone, and three years before the same region can be granted it again (Scotland 1997 to 2014,
  // Catalonia 2006 to 2017).
  "AutonomyRevokeRadicalism": 0.10,
  "AutonomyRegrantDays": 1095,
  // The computer grants only when overstretched or below 0.50 stability, to a region it has no
  // title to and at least this radical, at most once a quarter, and only with the points (1.5 times
  // the cost) and the money: the week must stay out of deficit, or the treasury hold this many weeks
  // of the price. It never takes a grant back.
  "AiAutonomyRadicalism": 0.15,
  "AiAutonomyIntervalDays": 90,
  "AiAutonomyReserveWeeks": 26,

  // ---- a proclaimed union of kindred peoples.
  // A people of the founder's family pays this share of UnionCohesionPerPeople when the union is
  // proclaimed: Yugoslavia's six South Slav peoples start at 0.70, above the trouble line 0.60,
  // instead of 0.40 and gone within the year. 1 restores the old price for everyone.
  "UnionCohesionKindredShare": 0.5
}
